      "writtenOn": "2023-05-10T18:21:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have a question around the usage of Settings.Global\n\nSince checkApmEnhancementEnabled is called at each bluetooth boot, the value stored in `Settings.Global` will be erase and re-write the previous value.\nSo what is the goal of setting this inside the Settings.Global ? Just to give acces to the Bluetooth config ?\n\nFor example if I use `adb shell cmd settings put global apm_enhancement_enabled 1` to modify this value, it does not persist.\n\n\n----\n\nLooking at the documentation of Settings.Global:\n\u003e these are for preferences that the user must explicitly modify through the system UI or specialized APIs for those values.\n\nI looked at the code and didn\u0027t found it.\nBut by looking at it, I found that the settings config is also used by wifi.\n\nAre you using this to have a global config shared between bluetooth and wifi ?\nIf this is the case, shouldn\u0027t we remove all this code in bluetooth and only set a default value in settings ? I found [this list](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/master/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml) of default value. Wouldn\u0027t it be  better to set apm_enhancement_enabled there instead ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1838,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 1839,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "d6b83b192a68c04d8e98f2814913420d6b7c6214",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b8ea39d_e3320d92",
